[36m(main_task pid=2489016)[0m The primary author of the Federalist Papers, a series of 85 essays written to advocate for the ratification of the United States Constitution, was Alexander Hamilton. However, James Madison and John Jay also contributed significantly to these papers.
[36m(main_task pid=2489016)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2489016)[0m The origin of the term "third wheel" is not definitively known. One popular theory suggests it originated in horse-drawn wagon terms, referring to the third wheel added to increase passenger capacity. Another theory points to beach wheelchairs where the third wheel helps with stability. A more recent idea links it to car radios of the 1930s. An old story from a Variety article in 1925 credits vaudeville performers Felix Fevers and Wally Wiggins for the phrase, describing the frustrated lead performer when a third comedian joined. The term has evolved to be used more generally to describe someone who feels like an unnecessary or awkward addition.
