[36m(main_task pid=2489016)[0m Doc 2(Title: "Names of Sri Lanka") Names of Sri Lanka Sri Lanka (Sinhala: ශ්‍රී ලංකා, ""Śrī Lankā""; Tamil: இலங்கை , ""Ilaṅkai""), officially the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka, is an island in the northern Indian Ocean which has been known under various names over time. Under British rule, the island was known as Ceylon from 1815-1972. ""Lanka"" was the classical name bestowed on the island by the Ramayana, an ancient Indian epic. A possible theory is that the name Lanka is derived from the Tamil word ""ilanku"" (இலங்கு), which means ""to shine"" or ""to glitter"", thus making ""Lanka"" a name that means ""that which glitters"".
[36m(main_task pid=2489016)[0m Doc 3(Title: "Sri Lanka Standard Time") Sri Lanka Standard Time Sri Lanka Standard Time (SLST) (Sinhala: ශ්‍රී ලංකාවේ සම්මත වේලාව ""Shri Lankavay Sammatha Velava"" Tamil: இலங்கை நியம ��ேகம் ""Ilaiy Nagam vegam"") is Sri Lanka's time zone, based on the meridian passing through the Observatory at the R.A.S.O., Kottawa. SLST is 5 hours and 30 minutes ahead of UTC, which is denoted as UTC +5:30, or +05:30. It has also been called Lankashilla in the past. Sri Lanka Standard Time is part of the Eastern and Southern Time zone. Sri Lanka Standard Time was established by the government of Sri Lanka to standardize the observance of timekeeping.
