[36m(main_task pid=2489016)[0m Doc 2(Title: tmaze) In two previous articles on linear tracing by a robotic arm [1, 2], the low level tracking was established on board using the QuickMat API. It was shown how various low level tracking algorithms from QuickMat can be used: PTV, WT, curvatures, etc. QuickMat is a mathematical tool-bench for applications in various fields of science such as signal and image analysis, computer vision and particle tracking velocimetry. It consists in a small collection of reliable numerical algorithms for image processing that were integrated into an Object Pascal library, through the VCL framework, that can be easily deployed in various programming environments, even outside the Windows platform (OSX and Linux). In this tutorial, we will build upon the QuickMat API for simple and clear examples of linear tracking problems with QuickMat. If you are still interested in reading QuickMat tutorials, more will follow.
